      "summary": {
        "headline": "Long-term trends and projections for all household mail, sent and received, show continuous volume declines across the study period.",
        "statements": [
          {
            "text": "For all households, household-mail-total fell by 39,500.0 millions of pieces, or 28.9 percent, from 2012 to 2023 across the FY2012 methodology break.",
            "metric": "household-mail-total",
            "years": [
              2012,
              2023
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "For all households, household-mail-total decreased by 36,500.0 millions of pieces, or 27.3 percent, from 2013 to 2023.",
            "metric": "household-mail-total",
            "years": [
              2013,
              2023
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "For all households, household-mail-total declined by 23,600.0 millions of pieces, or 19.5 percent, from 2018 to 2023.",
            "metric": "household-mail-total",
            "years": [
              2018,
              2023
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "For all households, household-mail-total went down by 8,500.0 millions of pieces, or 8.0 percent, from 2022 to 2023.",
            "metric": "household-mail-total",
            "years": [
              2022,
              2023
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "For all households, the projected household-mail-total is 93,809.0 millions of pieces in 2024 with an 80% prediction interval 87,358.0 to 100,260.0.",
            "metric": "household-mail-total",
            "years": [
              2024
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "For all households, the projected household-mail-total is 79,445.0 millions of pieces in 2028 with an 80% prediction interval 65,020.0 to 93,871.0.",
            "metric": "household-mail-total",
            "years": [
              2028
            ]
          }
        ],
        "caveats": [
          "Prior to 2007, Standard mail volumes were inflated by about 3 billion pieces due to a double count of Detached Address Labels in the Carrier Cost System, whose volumes are the control for the survey results.",
          "Volumes through 2007 were understated by about 2 to 3 billion pieces due to a change in the methodology used by the carrier cost system for estimating deliveries to residential addresses.",
          "Beginning in 2010, diary data were restated because of changes in weighting methodology.",
          "Beginning in 2012 data was restated due to weighing by Home Ownership.",
          "From the FY2024 report, results are published as pieces per household per year, and the survey contractor changed.",
          "FY2025 used a new survey design, renamed the Household Mail Survey, with changes to age bands and the definition of Large MSA."
        ]
